# Let Git decide what counts as text, and check every text file out with LF on
# every platform.
#
# Without this, core.autocrlf=true hands a Windows clone a CRLF working tree.
# Any test that reads a project file and matches it against a pattern holding a
# literal \n then fails locally while CI, which runs on LF, stays green — see
# tests/design-tokens.test.ts, where that silently disabled all 31 tests.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries: never rewrite the bytes.
*.png binary
*.ico binary
